# Git workflow

- Use Conventional Commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `docs:`, `ci:`.
- Subject line is imperative, under 72 characters, and says why the change exists.
- Before committing backend changes, run:

```powershell
dotnet build backend/LifeFitAI.sln --configuration Release
dotnet test backend/LifeFitAI.sln --configuration Release --no-build
```

- Before committing database changes, run `docker build -t lifefit-liquibase ./database`. When a local Liquibase CLI is configured, also run `liquibase validate` from `database/`.
- Before committing web changes, run `npm run lint` and `npm run build` in `web/`.
- Before committing mobile changes, run `npm run typecheck` in `mobile/`.
- Do not commit secrets, `.env`, user secrets, or real signing keys.
- Do not push, force-push, or amend unless the user asks.
